A||||10||theogre||Synthetic Oil: Best Pricing....||||10||
Z||000000||theogre||04-28-2001||07:43 PM||||I was at wall mart to day. I've always wanted to use Mobil 1 but the stuff is so bloody expencive and I'm always really tight on cash.<P>Anyway, Today I figured I'd treat myself and get it anyway. (Ogres just have to do that every so often.) So I grabbed 5 quarts off the shelf.... (I always get an extra unless I already have extra of what ever it is I'm using....)<P>Then I turned the corner at the other end of the row and saw an endcap I didn't see earlier.... Big 5 quart Mobil 1 bottles for &lt;$18. The 5 loose quarts I had in the cart were $4.29 each.... <P>needless to say I dumped them and got the 5Q bottle.<P>Even if I don't use the extra quart before next change, I can save them. When I get 4 extras I'll have a whole Mobil 1 oil change for free compared to the price of loose quarts.<P>I also tried one of those orange "6 in 1" filter wrenches. It works but I'm not sure if I like it. It's nice to have one wrench that fits the Fiero and the Caravan but the thing is kind of kludgy. It als won't work well on Fram filters with the black grip coating. <P>------------------<BR><I><B>Screamin Yellow Zonkers... If it's Screamin and Yellow, I ain't eatin it.</B></I>||||reg||10
Z||000001||RossT||04-28-2001||07:50 PM||||I talked to a guy from walmart about the mobil 1 promotion (5 quart jug).  He said that about twice a year they run that promotion.  The 5 quart jugs usually sell out fast, so stock up.  But one thing that I found out is that after the promotion is over, the price on the 1 qt bottle drops!!<P>still a good buy!! I try to stock up..<P>Ross<P>[This message has been edited by RossT (edited 04-28-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by RossT (edited 04-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||04-28-2001||09:19 PM||||I have the 6 in 1 filter wrench, but they should call it a 1 out of 6 instead. I have only found a couple of cars that it actually fits. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||stimpy||04-28-2001||09:26 PM||||For $27 you can get the oil, the filter, and a toothless grease monkey to change it for you. Wal-Mart, what a country!||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroJoe||04-28-2001||10:27 PM||||I've never had to use an oil filter wrench on my Fiero.  I can usually get a good grip on the filter if I'm wearing gloves.  <P>------------------<BR>AIM: FieroJoe87<BR>87 Coupe 5spd<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||04-28-2001||11:43 PM||||I'm not real impressed with the 6 in 1. It fit both filters (regular painted jobs). It got them off with less BS than normal. At least is was cheap...<P>I think I'll just get a couple spring caps and be done with it. Those things will grab anything.<P>As for the $27 oil change.... no chance. Plus that's just regular crude base oil. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||stimpy||04-29-2001||10:37 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by theogre:<BR><B><BR>As for the $27 oil change.... no chance. Plus that's just regular crude base oil. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ahh, skeptics! $11 gets you the Pennzoil. I watch said grease monkey pull the Mobil one off the shelf, ring it up on the register, and pour it in my car. If they are sneaking regular crude oil in there somewhere and passing it off as Mobil 1, how do you really know what was in that big ol 6 qt bottle?  Ask Patrick, I know how to argue this point!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||GT GT 87||04-29-2001||02:16 PM||||Mobil one is the best!!!! I believe it is the only oil with a MIL-  number  for the military.  They use it in the space shuttle  , the Ageis class Missle cruiser  With turbines out of a DC-10.  ,,and of course the M-1   A- 1   battle tank..   I let my miles go an extra 1000 miles before changing ,, it is still good.  BUT no more than that. I have a longer story but I don't like typing!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fiero_Freak||04-29-2001||11:45 PM||||I ran the sythetic wal-mart brand once.  It didn't seem to break down too much about the same as using Mobile1.  But I had one little leak, before and after Mobile 1.  I started using that Valvoline over 75K stuff and it's works great!  No leaks at all.  ||||reg||1
Z||000009||thomas_l||04-30-2001||10:54 AM||||I just changed with Castrol Syntec 5w-50 on my 166k 2.8L. It runs smoother and quieted down a little bearing chatter at &gt;3500 rpm. We'll see how it does over time, as this 87 GT will be mainly stuffed in the front of my garage to be taken out every few weeks for autocross abuse.<P>My favorite oil filter wrench is my giant 18" channel-lock pliers. It fits anything up to about 6-7" in diameter. Who cares if the old filter gets a little crushed - and the new one should go on only hand tight anyway.||||reg||10
Z||000010||mrgone||04-30-2001||11:06 AM||||naw, the best oil filter grabber is a c-clamp<BR>got the thang off good, you.||||reg||1
